According to a commonly used meter, house prices have risen most to seven years in Australia's winter months.
RP Data CoreLogic Hedonic, a price index of RP Data CoreLogic Hedonic, which measures house prices in the Australian capital, rose by 1.1 per cent in August, according to RP data on Monday.
With the ascension over the course of June, July and August, price increases totalled 4.2 per cent, i.e. higher than in the same months after 2007.
The annual price increase was 10.9 per cent, which is more than twice as high in the 12 months prior to August 2013, but prices have not risen evenly across the country.
