RP Data's results show that house prices rose 16.1 per cent in Sydney and 12.7 per cent in Melbourne the previous year.
A housing market for Adelaide, Brisbane and Darwin is the next busiest; an average price rise is between five and six per cent.
The weakest housing market lies in Canberra, where prices went up just 1.4 per cent a year as a result of government spending cuts.
